H1('13. Interview Preparation')
S += [P('30-second version','H2X'), P('This project centralizes GitHub repository access. Spring Boot syncs data from GitHub into PostgreSQL, Next.js presents dashboards and workflows, and administrators map GitHub users to employees and remove access during offboarding. The design records jobs, approvals, and audit events and runs with Docker.')]
S += [P('3-minute version','H2X'), P('The browser talks to Next.js, which provides both server-rendered pages and same-origin API routes. Those route handlers call Spring Boot over HTTP. Spring controllers are thin; services contain sync, employee, governance, and offboarding rules; Spring Data repositories persist JPA entities in PostgreSQL. During sync, the backend pages through repositories and collaborators from GitHub, asks GitHub for each permission, then uses an isolated transaction per repository to upsert the repository and GitHub users and replace access rows. Employee mappings add the human identity layer. Removal workflows call GitHub first and only then remove local access, recording partial failures and audit events. Bulk offboarding creates a governance approval; approval synchronously executes an offboarding job per employee. Docker Compose coordinates PostgreSQL, backend, and frontend, and an optional Nginx proxy. The strongest design ideas are explicit workflow records and per-unit transactions. The main production gaps are incomplete authentication enforcement, no versioned migrations, duplicated GitHub policy calls, weak default secrets, and inconsistent error handling.')]
qa=[
('Why Spring Boot?','It provides REST, dependency injection, JPA repositories, and transaction control with little infrastructure code.'),('Why RepositoryAccess?','It models the many-to-many relationship and stores permission, source, and sync time.'),('Why REQUIRES_NEW?','One repository or removal can commit/fail independently, enabling partial success.'),('How is consistency handled with GitHub?','Remote deletion happens before local deletion. Failures are recorded, but there is no distributed transaction or compensation.'),('How does sync avoid stale rows?','It deletes and recreates access rows per repository and marks repositories absent from the current fetch inactive.'),('What is the N+1 risk?','Sync requests each collaborator permission separately; entity graphs may also trigger many relationship queries.'),('How would you scale sync?','Queue repository tasks, cap concurrency, batch permission retrieval where possible, checkpoint jobs, and respect rate limits.'),('Is it secure?','It has signed cookies and server-side PATs, but API authentication and Spring Security are missing; it needs hardening.'),('How are schemas migrated?','Currently Hibernate update and Prisma db push. A production design should choose one owner and committed migrations.'),('How are failures exposed?','Jobs and items store statuses/errors; most API exceptions become 400; read failures may become empty data.'),('What does approval do?','For BULK_OFFBOARDING it changes batch state and immediately executes the batch synchronously.'),('Where is RBAC?','A role string exists, but no authorization rule uses it.'),('Why two ORMs?','Spring uses JPA for the backend; Prisma defines/types the shared schema and is used in a few Next operations. This increases drift risk.'),('How are duplicates prevented?','Unique GitHub username/repo ID and unique repository-user access; employee email uniqueness is application-enforced only.'),('What tests exist?','One Spring integration test covers health, sync-to-offboarding, bulk approval, and permission validation with a mocked GitHub client.'),('What would you improve first?','Enforce auth end-to-end, adopt migrations, centralize errors/DTO validation, then remove duplicated integration logic.'),('Is GITHUB_OWNER used?','It is configured but repository discovery calls /user/repos, so the verified runtime does not filter by owner.'),('How are rate limits handled?','A single retry waits until the reset timestamp only for 403 with zero remaining.'),('What is the API style?','REST-like JSON resources plus action endpoints such as /execute and /remove-all.'),('How is audit detail stored?','AuditLogService serializes a details map to PostgreSQL JSON through Hibernate.')]
S += [P('Likely interview questions','H2X'),table(['Question','Grounded answer'],qa,[57*mm,125*mm],tiny=True)]

